and hence complete the proof of the following statement using the axioms $[\\text{A}1]-[\\text{A}8]$ given below.\n\n*Statement:*\n\n*If $w$ and $v$ are vectors such that $x+w=v+x$ for some $x\\in V$, then $w=v.$*\n\n*Proof:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+w & =v+x &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ (x+w)+(-x) & =(v+x)+(-x) &  & [\\,\\text{add }-x\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ (w+x)+(-x) & =(v+x)+(-x) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,] \\\\ w+(x+(-x)) & =v+(x+(-x)) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A2}\\,] \\\\ w+0 & =v+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,] \\\\ w & =v &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A3}\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe axioms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{[A1]}:x+y=y+x & \\text{[A5]}:1\\cdot x=x \\\\ \\text{[A2]}:(x+y)+z=x+(y+z) & \\text{[A6]}:\\alpha (\\beta x)=(\\alpha \\beta )x \\\\ \\text{[A3]}:x+0=x & \\text{[A7]}:(\\alpha +\\beta )x=\\alpha x+\\beta x \\\\ \\text{[A4]}:x+(-x)=0 & \\text{[A8]}:\\alpha (x+y)=\\alpha x+\\alpha y\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the vector space axioms, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+w & =v+x &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ (x+w)+(-x) & =(v+x)+(-x) &  & [\\,\\text{add }-x\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ (w+x)+(-x) & =(v+x)+(-x) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A1}\\,] \\\\ w+(x+(-x)) & =v+(x+(-x)) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A2}\\,] \\\\ w+0 & =v+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A4}\\,] \\\\ w & =v &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A3}\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184764 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184167 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9bdb6bc9-47e2-5330-a1ee-270882f2aced" :knowledge-point/title "Proving Statements Using the Vector Space Axioms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "54174a8e-4b9f-5398-9c3e-042309cf5af7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A1}$, $\\text{A3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418998} {:answer/id #uuid "7c55b42e-8e25-5d4a-9c6c-fb23853f6637" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A4}$, $\\text{A3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419001} {:answer/id #uuid "923e4cd4-7cb7-513f-a013-6b459182a21c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A5}$, $\\text{A4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419002} {:answer/id #uuid "c5a112ad-76a7-5358-b6fe-7be7dc9072ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A3}$, $\\text{A4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419003} {:answer/id #uuid "edaa960c-9666-5ef7-ae8f-8608f1b827e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A1}$, $\\text{A2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419004}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "54174a8e-4b9f-5398-9c3e-042309cf5af7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A1}$, $\\text{A3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418998} :answer-field/id #uuid "90535267-04a3-5209-88fc-9a5564318779" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183193}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "19147c4b-722c-5ed5-9d91-8a4847b759ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-35626" :question/problem "From top to bottom, fill in the blanks and hence complete the proof of the following statement using the axioms $[\\text{A}1]-[\\text{A}8]$ given below.\n\n*Statement:*\n\n*If $w$ is a vector such that $x+w=x$ for some $x\\in V$, then $w=0.$*\n\n*Proof:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+w & =x &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ (x+w)+(-x) & =x+(-x) &  & [\\,\\text{add }-x\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ (w+x)+(-x) & =x+(-x) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,] \\\\ w+(x+(-x)) & =x+(-x) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A2}\\,] \\\\ w+0 & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A4}\\,] \\\\ w & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe axioms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{[A1]}:x+y=y+x & \\text{[A5]}:1\\cdot x=x \\\\ \\text{[A2]}:(x+y)+z=x+(y+z) & \\text{[A6]}:\\alpha (\\beta x)=(\\alpha \\beta )x \\\\ \\text{[A3]}:x+0=x & \\text{[A7]}:(\\alpha +\\beta )x=\\alpha x+\\beta x \\\\ \\text{[A4]}:x+(-x)=0 & \\text{[A8]}:\\alpha (x+y)=\\alpha x+\\alpha y\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the vector space axioms, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+w & =x &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ (x+w)+(-x) & =x+(-x) &  & [\\,\\text{add }-x\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ (w+x)+(-x) & =x+(-x) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A1}\\,] \\\\ w+(x+(-x)) & =x+(-x) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A2}\\,] \\\\ w+0 & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A4}\\,] \\\\ w & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A3}\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423671 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184196 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d9b62ae-7545-5d65-bcf7-74ab0e8662ec" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sets That Are Not Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c610fab-a6ec-5612-9143-78410e0c0685" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "addition of matrices in $T$ is not associative" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423660} {:answer/id #uuid "952805ec-db79-5003-ab44-c608da27648b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "there exists a matrix $A\\in T$ such that $A+B\\ne O$ for any $B\\in T.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423662} {:answer/id #uuid "97a1f3dc-dc3c-53f9-b457-30bca1c9f80b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$T$ does not contain the zero matrix $O$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423663} {:answer/id #uuid "d008fb5f-392d-5a1e-8353-f48e8e0933c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "addition of matrices in $T$ is not commutative" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423665} {:answer/id #uuid "f89006ab-36a7-5769-850c-8ee5d58a71d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "multiplication by a scalar is not closed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423667}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f89006ab-36a7-5769-850c-8ee5d58a71d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "multiplication by a scalar is not closed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423667} :answer-field/id #uuid "047ee837-df71-5e5c-bcee-335a715a816d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423668}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "87c89c45-3edb-5cd5-88f1-a3ee2b4d8003" :question/math-academy-id "q-35640" :question/problem "Let $T$ be the set of all $2\\times 2$ matrices $({a}_{ij})$  with real entries, such that  ${a}_{11}+{a}_{22}$ is rational.  Complete the following sentence:\n\n*$T$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to addition of matrices and multiplication of matrices by a real number) because $\\text{____}\\,.$*" :question/worked-solution "The correct answer is \n\n*$T$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to addition of matrices and multiplication of matrices by a real number) because **multiplication by a scalar is not closed.** *\n\n For example, the identity matrix \n\n$$\nI=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nlies in $T$, but\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{2}\\cdot I=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]\\notin T\n$$\n\nbecause $\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{2}$ is not a rational number.\n\nOn the other hand,\n\n- The zero matrix belongs to $T.$  $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition of matrices with real entries is commutative, in general.    $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition of matrices with real entries is associative, in general.    $\\,✓$\n\n- Given any $A\\in T,$  the additive inverse matrix $-A=(-1)\\cdot A$ is also in  $T,$ and   $A+(-A)=O.$  $\\,✓$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419007 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184196 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d9b62ae-7545-5d65-bcf7-74ab0e8662ec" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sets That Are Not Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "313cdc82-5d69-5af4-95bb-ace914a012ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "multiplication of $f\\in A$ by a scalar is not closed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418996} {:answer/id #uuid "4f43eb35-6698-556b-937a-7540b2eaa194" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "addition of functions in $A$  is not associative" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418997} {:answer/id #uuid "54d7d70f-b06b-5dba-8920-ce4be2335648" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "addition of functions in $A$  is not commutative" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418999} {:answer/id #uuid "61ff392f-4de3-5c34-9123-789573d772b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1\\cdot f\\ne f$ for some $f\\in A$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419000} {:answer/id #uuid "f187a6fa-78fb-565f-9a52-c1915abb65f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "addition and scalar multiplication of functions  in $A$ do not satisfy the distributive laws" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419005}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "313cdc82-5d69-5af4-95bb-ace914a012ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "multiplication of $f\\in A$ by a scalar is not closed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418996} :answer-field/id #uuid "4628fceb-08d9-5ba5-86ad-00d444e18706" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419006}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1a47334c-0a05-5b9c-b7eb-76cf4c1d5cfb" :question/math-academy-id "q-94792" :question/problem "Let $A$ be the set of all functions $f:R\\to R$ of the form  $f(x)=a+{x}^{2},$ where $a\\in R.$ Complete the following sentence:\n\n*$A$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to function addition and scalar multiplication) because $\\text{_________}\\,.$*" :question/worked-solution "The correct answer is as follows:\n\n*$A$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to function addition and scalar multiplication) because **multiplication of $f\\in A$ by a scalar is not closed.** *\n\nFor example, if $\\alpha =2$ and $f(x)={x}^{2},$ then $\\alpha f(x)=2{x}^{2}.$ So, $\\alpha f(x)\\notin A$ because the coefficient of ${x}^{2}$ is not $1.$\n\nOn the other hand:\n\n- Addition of real valued functions  is associative. $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition and scalar multiplication of polynomials satisfy the distributive laws.\n$\\,✓$\n\n- Addition of real valued functions  is commutative. $\\,✓$\n\n- $1\\cdot f=f$ for all $f\\in A.$ $\\,✓$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360505 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184196 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d9b62ae-7545-5d65-bcf7-74ab0e8662ec" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sets That Are Not Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "148e1662-35f6-5380-bc45-570bd123aa65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "addition and scalar multiplication of matrices do not satisfy the distributive laws" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357930} {:answer/id #uuid "320b5d11-4a8f-55fe-bba8-195d9e922e5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "addition of matrices is not commutative" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358197} {:answer/id #uuid "48109943-1239-5a7c-af98-06bb37c313df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the $2\\times 1$  zero matrix does not belong to $K$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358370} {:answer/id #uuid "7d249c29-f44d-5240-8308-3b4e8b179337" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "addition of matrices is not associative" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358839} {:answer/id #uuid "db7e8f9f-3fef-596d-bd51-f3eb1ae8d92d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1\\cdot A\\ne A$ for all $A\\in K$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359674}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "48109943-1239-5a7c-af98-06bb37c313df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the $2\\times 1$  zero matrix does not belong to $K$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358370} :answer-field/id #uuid "115fee41-7a55-5085-8c7d-272bb27890fe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360027}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ec097acf-f56e-507d-aaff-ec7126bba2f2" :question/math-academy-id "q-94807" :question/problem "Let $K$ be the set of all $2\\times 1$ matrices $[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],$ such that $x,y\\in R$ and $x+y=1.$  Complete the following sentence:\n\n*$K$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to matrix addition and scalar multiplication) because $\\text{_________}\\,.$*" :question/worked-solution "The correct answer is as follows:\n\n*$K$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to matrix addition and scalar multiplication) because **the $2\\times 1$  zero matrix does not belong to $K.$** *  \n\nIndeed, adding the entries of the $2\\times 1$  zero matrix yields $0+0=0\\ne 1.$\n\nOn the other hand:\n\n- addition of matrices is associative. $\\,✓$\n\n- addition and scalar multiplication of matrices  satisfy the distributive laws. $✓$\n\n- Addition of matrices  is commutative. $\\,✓$\n\n- $1\\cdot A=A$ for all $A\\in K.$ $\\,✓$"}]}
